+SOURCE
+ProofIdentityAudit.lean
+
+COMMAND
+lake env lean ProofIdentityAudit.lean
+
+WORKING DIRECTORY
+/tmp/audit-work/stage5-fresh
+
+ENVIRONMENT
+LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/proc-self-readlink.so
+LAKE_HOME=/tmp/audit-work/lake-home
+LEAN_SYSROOT=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0
+LAKE_OVERRIDE_LEAN=true
+
+EXIT
+0
+
+EXACT OUTPUT
+Proof.final :
+  Klean38DecodeCyclic.Lemmas.targetStatement Proof.«_<=Int_» Proof.«Map:update»
+    Proof.«lengthString(_)_STRING-COMMON_Int_String» Proof.«substrString(_,_,_)_STRING-COMMON_String_String_Int_Int»
+theorem Proof.final : Klean38DecodeCyclic.Lemmas.targetStatement Proof.«_<=Int_» Proof.«Map:update»
+  Proof.«lengthString(_)_STRING-COMMON_Int_String» Proof.«substrString(_,_,_)_STRING-COMMON_String_String_Int_Int» :=
+⟨fun V' K M V =>
+  {
+    mp := fun h =>
+      have hcoll := congrArg SortMap.coll h;
+      Eq.mp
+        (Eq.trans
+          (Eq.trans
+            (congr
+              (congrArg (fun x => Eq { coll := (K, V) :: List.filter x M.coll }.coll)
+                (funext fun entry => Classical.decide_not (entry.fst = K)))
+              (congrArg (fun x => { coll := (K, V') :: List.filter x M.coll }.coll)
+                (funext fun entry => Classical.decide_not (entry.fst = K))))
+            (List.cons.injEq (K, V) (List.filter (fun entry => !decide (entry.fst = K)) M.coll) (K, V')
+              (List.filter (fun entry => !decide (entry.fst = K)) M.coll)))
+          (Eq.trans
+            (congr
+              (congrArg And
+                (Eq.trans (Prod.mk.injEq K V K V')
+                  (Eq.trans (congrArg (fun x => x ∧ V = V') (eq_self K)) (true_and (V = V')))))
+              (eq_self (List.filter (fun entry => !decide (entry.fst = K)) M.coll)))
+            (and_true (V = V'))))
+        hcoll,
+    mpr := fun h => h ▸ Eq.refl (Proof.«Map:update» M K V) },
+  ⟨fun S =>
+    of_eq_true
+      (Eq.trans
+        (congrArg (fun x => x = true)
+          (Eq.trans
+            ((fun p p_1 e_p =>
+                @Eq.rec Prop p (fun p_2 e_p => ∀ {h : Decidable p} [h_1 : Decidable p_2], decide p = decide p_2)
+                  (fun {h} [h_1 : Decidable p] => Subsingleton.elim h h_1 ▸ Eq.refl (decide p)) p_1 e_p)
+              (0 ≤ Proof.«lengthString(_)_STRING-COMMON_Int_String» S) True
+              (Int.ofNat_zero_le._simp_1 (String.length S)))
+            (decide_true instDecidableTrue)))
+        (eq_self true)),
+    fun S =>
+    String.casesOn (motive := fun t =>
+      S = t →
+        Proof.«substrString(_,_,_)_STRING-COMMON_String_String_Int_Int» S 0
+            (Proof.«lengthString(_)_STRING-COMMON_Int_String» S) =
+          S)
+      S
+      (fun data h =>
+        Eq.symm h ▸
+          of_eq_true
+            (Eq.trans
+              (congrArg (fun x => { data := x } = { data := data })
+                (Eq.trans (congrArg (fun x => List.take x.toNat data) (Int.sub_zero ↑data.length)) List.take_length))
+              (eq_self { data := data })))
+      (Eq.refl S)⟩⟩
diff --git a/evidence/09-operational-bridge.log b/evidence/09-operational-bridge.log
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a4772579595adce7cee185f5d47a87bb273526ce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/09-operational-bridge.log
@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+K PROBE SOURCE
+string-probe.k
+
+K BUILD COMMAND
+kompile string-probe.k --backend haskell --main-module STRING-PROBE --syntax-module STRING-PROBE --output-definition string-probe-valid-kompiled
+
+EXIT
+0
+
+K RUN COMMAND SHAPE
+krun --definition string-probe-valid-kompiled -cPGM=<closed-token>
+
+EXACT RESULTS
+lenEmpty EXIT 0
+<k>
+  0 ~> .K
+</k>
+
+lenAscii EXIT 0
+<k>
+  3 ~> .K
+</k>
+
+lenAccent EXIT 0
+<k>
+  1 ~> .K
+</k>
+
+lenAstral EXIT 0
+<k>
+  1 ~> .K
+</k>
+
+lenCombining EXIT 0
+<k>
+  2 ~> .K
+</k>
+
+subFull EXIT 0
+<k>
+  "abcdef" ~> .K
+</k>
+
+subMiddle EXIT 0
+<k>
+  "bcd" ~> .K
+</k>
+
+subUnicode EXIT 0
+<k>
+  "\xf0\x9f\x99\x82\xe9" ~> .K
+</k>
+
+The K pretty printer's escaped subUnicode result represents the two compiled
+K characters 🙂 and é. The closed compiled literals avoid the known direct
+-c string serialization distortion.
+
+subEmpty EXIT 0
+<k>
+  "" ~> .K
+</k>
+
+INVALID CONSTANT DIAGNOSTIC
+Adding the closed term substrString("abcdef", -1, 2) made kompile exit 113:
+
+[Error] Compiler: Argument to hook STRING.substr out of range. Expected a
+32-bit unsigned integer.
+  while executing phase "constant expression folding"
+
+The frozen program never invokes substring outside
+0 <= start <= end <= length, due semantic.k lines 112-129. The candidate's
+total Lean extension outside that operational domain is therefore not used as
+evidence.
+
+LEAN PROBE SOURCE
+OperationalAudit.lean
+
+LEAN COMMAND
+lake env lean OperationalAudit.lean
+
+EXIT
+0
+
+EXACT OUTPUT
+true
+true
+false
+0
+3
+1
+1
+2
+"abcdef"
+"bcd"
+"🙂é"
+""
+
+The silent checked examples additionally establish:
+
+1. Updating an existing key preserves the unrelated binding and overwrites
+   exactly that key.
+2. Updating a fresh key preserves both existing bindings.
+3. The generated target is also provable for counterfactual bad definitions:
+   constant-true comparison, singleton/discarding map update, constant-zero
+   length, and identity substring.
+4. The actual candidate differs from each of those bad definitions on a
+   concrete adversarial example.
+
+Thus the target equation alone is not treated as bridge evidence. The actual
+definitions pass independent operational comparison: Int order is exact;
+map update overwrites one key and preserves the remainder; length counts K
+characters for ASCII, BMP, astral, and combining cases; substring uses the
+same valid half-open character indices as the frozen rules.
